<Legal
  title="Data Deletion"
  description="How to have your personal information deleted from TradeCommand."
  updated="27 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    You can have the personal information TradeCommand holds about you deleted. Which route applies
    depends on how your information reached us.
  </p>

  <h2>If you have a TradeCommand account</h2>
  <p>
    In the TradeCommand app or at app.tradecommand.com.au, open your profile and choose
    <strong>Delete account</strong>. You confirm with your password, and we delete the account
    straight away.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also email <a href="mailto:privacy@tradecommand.com.au">privacy@tradecommand.com.au</a> from the
    address on your account and ask us to delete it. We confirm the request, then delete your account
    and the personal information attached to it within 30 days.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are the only owner of a business, deleting your account deletes the business and its
    records too. If the business has other owners, it continues and only your account is deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>If a business entered your details</h2>
  <p>
    A trade business that uses TradeCommand may have entered your details as a client or contact,
    or received a message you sent it. That business controls those records. Ask the business to
    delete them, or email us and we will pass the request on and confirm the outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>If you connected through Facebook or WhatsApp</h2>
  <p>
    If you signed in or connected a WhatsApp Business account through Facebook Login, you can remove
    the connection from your Facebook settings under <strong>Apps and Websites</strong>. Removing
    TradeCommand there revokes our access. To delete the data we already hold, email us as above and
    include the phone number or account name you connected.
  </p>

  <h2>What deletion covers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account, name, email address and phone number.</li>
    <li>Messages, files and records attached to your account.</li>
    <li>Access tokens for any service you connected.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We keep records the law requires us to keep, such as tax records, for the period the law sets.
    Backups expire on their own cycle within 90 days.
  </p>

  <p>
    Read our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for the full picture of what we collect and why.
  </p>
</Legal>
